From d0bb57f5dcff06d62a3c2ad855883c642be4afaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:09:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Alt+Tab: Window Maker's switch panel (icons, title,
 Esc/Enter/arrows)

The task list showed a debug list (title, [pid: cmdline] (pointer)) in a
dark box. It is now drawn as Window Maker's switch panel (switchpanel.c):
the windows' icons in a row (64-pixel icons in 77-pixel tiles, 10-pixel
border), the selected one in a darker tile with a white rounded frame, its
title in a dark strip below; gray panel with a black frame; minimized
windows dimmed; the row scrolls when there are more windows than fit.

Icons (new app_icon.c): the window's desktop entry (app ID, or the entry
whose StartupWMClass is the X11 class), looked up in the user's icon theme
(GTK settings.ini), the themes it inherits, hicolor and pixmaps; PNG or
SVG (librsvg); cached per application, also misses; a raised tile with the
title's initial when there is none.

Keys while the panel is shown, as on Window Maker: Esc cancels and returns
to the window active when the cycle began; Enter confirms; Left/Right move;
Home/End go to the first/last window. They no longer reach the application
under the panel (key grab, released when the panel closes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
